# punused findings adjudicated for this repo. One literal substring per line,
# matched against punused's output line; full-line `#` comments carry the
# reason. Invalid-by-construction classes: `.kiro/steering/tools.md`.
#
# web-terminal-engine is a LIBRARY that ships a `main` package
# (internal/e2etestserver), so cplieger/ci's app-mode detection ("a main package
# exists") gates it on punused -- but its exported surface is a PUBLISHED Go
# proxy API (github.com/cplieger/web-terminal-engine/v3), consumed by vibekit,
# web-terminal-kiro and web-terminal-server. punused's own README states it "does
# not detect references from outside of your project", and run.go asks gopls for
# `textDocument/references` scoped to this module only, so EVERY symbol a
# consumer repo calls reads as unused here. Triage therefore follows the library
# rules in tools.md, not the app rules: nothing is deleted on punused's word.
#
# The EU1001 ("used in test only") vs EU1002 ("no reference found") split below
# reflects only whether THIS repo's own tests happen to exercise the symbol --
# run.go skips `_test.go` files when collecting declarations but still counts
# references from them. It carries no information about consumer use.
#
# Patterns are symbol-only (no file:line), matching the nine sibling repos'
# files, so they survive line shifts in an actively edited file. Each entry was
# verified to match exactly one of the 29 findings.

