# --- Embedded struct types (invalid by construction). vt/screen.go:78-79 embed
# ParserState (vt/types.go:83) and CursorState (vt/screen.go:208) into Screen.
# Both have entirely unexported members, reached through the outer type:
# s.pState at vt/parse.go:29, s.oscBuf at vt/osc.go:84, s.curX/s.curY across
# vt/csi.go. punused asks gopls for references at the EMBED identifier, which
# resolves to the field, and a promoted-member access is not a reference to the
# field -- so satisfying this finding would mean writing s.ParserState.pState
# everywhere, which is strictly worse Go. Proof of the mechanism: the third
# embed on the same lines, altScreenState (vt/screen.go:217), is identical in
# every respect except its lowercase initial, and punused does not report it.
field ParserState
field CursorState

# --- Exported methods on an UNEXPORTED type. scrollbackRing (terminal/
# scrollback.go:22) is reachable only through Handler.scrollback, an unexported
# field (terminal/terminal.go:312), so no consumer can name the type or reach
# these methods -- exportedness is a red herring here (tools.md). Both are live
# in-repo observation points for real behavior, not accessors under test:
# Len is how TestED3ClearsScrollbackRing (terminal/scrollback_clear_test.go:16)
# proves CSI 3 J empties the ring while committed stays monotonic -- the
# regression guard for the resize-duplication bug -- and how the fuzz invariant
# at terminal/scrollback_fuzz_test.go:44 checks retention against capacity.
# Lines is the ring-order oracle for terminal/scrollback_test.go:24,41,66 and
# the commit checks at terminal/terminal_test.go:329 and
# terminal/flush_scheduler_test.go:233. Reading r.count/r.buf directly instead
# would reimplement the ring's index arithmetic inside its own tests.
method (*scrollbackRing).Len
method (*scrollbackRing).Lines

