# NewOriginPolicy, WithOriginPolicy and WithManagerOriginPolicy -- the
# cross-origin widening surface, successor to the removed WithAcceptOptions
# (which sat here for the same reason). Still no fleet caller, and that is the
# CORRECT posture rather than an oversight: every consumer serves its terminal
# same-origin, so all three deliberately rely on the same-origin default and
# web-terminal-kiro/routes_test.go asserts in prose that the app does not widen
# it. The API exists because the default cannot be widened any other way and
# net/http.CrossOriginProtection cannot do it (a WS handshake is a GET, which it
# treats as safe). Covered in-repo by TestNewHandler_WithOriginPolicy
# (terminal/terminal_options_test.go) and terminal/origin_test.go.
#
# WithOriginPolicy is NOT a substring of WithManagerOriginPolicy, so the two
# entries claim one finding each regardless of order.
function NewOriginPolicy
function WithManagerOriginPolicy
function WithOriginPolicy

